GERDA federal election data: CC BY 4.0

The processed GERDA federal election datasets at municipality, county, and
constituency level, together with the GERDA database compilation and accompanying
documentation for those datasets, are licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0), to the extent that the GERDA
maintainers hold the relevant rights. This covers both harmonized and
unharmonized federal election datasets, whether downloaded directly or accessed
through the gerda R package, an API, or an MCP server.

You may copy, redistribute, adapt, and use the covered material commercially,
subject to the license terms. Give appropriate credit to GERDA, retain supplied
attribution and license notices, link to CC BY 4.0, and indicate any changes.
Attribution must not suggest that the GERDA authors endorse you or your use.
Do not impose additional legal or technological restrictions on the rights
granted by the license.

Full license terms:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Required GERDA citation:
Heddesheimer, Vincent, Hanno Hilbig, Florian Sichart, and Andreas Wiedemann.
2025. "GERDA: The German Election Database." Scientific Data 12: 618.
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-04811-5

GERDA: https://www.german-elections.com/

Scope and third-party materials

This notice makes the federal-data reuse statement approved on September 17,
2026 explicit at the repository root. See mcp_server/DATA_REUSE_STATEMENT.md.
It does not establish or change the license for other election datasets,
candidate data, INKAR or other covariates, shapefiles, crosswalk source files,
or other third-party materials. Consult their documentation and original
providers' terms. Source materials remain subject to applicable original
provider terms, including attribution requirements; this notice grants only
rights held by the GERDA maintainers.

Software

This data license does not license the software in this repository. The gerda
R package is maintained separately at https://github.com/hhilbig/gerda and
declares an MIT license for its software. Using the package to download data
does not change the data's license or any applicable third-party terms.

Warranty

The covered material is provided as is, without warranty, as set out in
